1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:07,100
克拉克森：今晚，
乔丹开着我们的利亚纳闹出了大笑话，
CLARKSON: Tonight,
Jordan makes a boob in our Liana,

2
00:00:08,833 --> 00:00:12,233
法拉利与保时捷在我们的赛道上大打出手，
Ferrari and Porsche go to war on our track,

3
00:00:12,267 --> 00:00:15,267
还有，我们要故意撞几回车。
And we have some crashes, on purpose.

4
00:00:19,533 --> 00:00:21,767
观众朋友们晚上好，欢迎收看。
Hello, good evening and welcome.

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,333
话说，最近一直有人跟我们念叨，
Now, a number of people
have been saying

6
00:00:23,367 --> 00:00:26,733
说我们节目里又快又贵的豪车
实在太多了。
that there are too many
fast and expensive cars
on this show.

7
00:00:26,767 --> 00:00:30,800
于是，摄制组出了个鬼点子。
So, the production team
came up with a plan.

8
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:33,433
他们给每位主持人发了100英镑。
They gave each
of the presenters £100.

9
00:00:33,467 --> 00:00:35,733
然后让我们各凭本事去买辆车。
And we were told
to go off and buy a car.

10
00:00:35,767 --> 00:00:40,333
而且必须是合法合规能上路的车，
预算不能超过100块。
That's a road legal car
for less than 100 quid.

11
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:42,967
接着让我们在M1高速旁的
托丁顿服务区集合，
Then we were told to meet up
at Toddington Services,

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,800
在那里等待我们的是
一系列严峻挑战。
on the M1 where we would be
given a number of challenges.

13
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:49,000
事情是这样的。
This is what happened.

14
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,967
克拉克森：
我是第一个到的，座驾就是……嘿，瞧瞧这玩意儿！
CLARKSON:
I was the first to arrive
with... Well, look at it!

15
00:01:00,067 --> 00:01:03,133
整整两吨
瑞典工业的绝世杰作！
Two tonnes
of Swedish magnificence!

16
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:08,067
沃尔沃760。
It's the Volvo 760.

17
00:01:08,067 --> 00:01:11,533
搭载2.8升
V6发动机。
It has the 2.8 litre,
V6 engine.

18
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:13,067
而且还是高配GLE版。
And it's the GLE model.

19
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:16,433
电动天窗、
真皮座椅、空调，一应俱全。
So, electric sunshine roof,
leather, air conditioning.

20
00:01:16,467 --> 00:01:17,800
车况居然还不赖。
And it's not in bad neck.

21
00:01:17,833 --> 00:01:19,267
肉眼看不见一丝锈蚀。
No corrosion that I can see.

22
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,500
也没有任何值当一提的凹坑或划痕。
No dents and scratches
worth talking about.

23
00:01:21,533 --> 00:01:24,833
路税和年检居然
都还有整整两个月才到期。
It's actually taxed and tested
for another two months.

24
00:01:24,867 --> 00:01:26,833
接着就是詹姆斯买回来的东西了。
And that's what James
has bought.

25
00:01:26,867 --> 00:01:28,567
他来了。
Here he is.

26
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,300
说实话这车看着比我的还现代，
我挺不甘心的，不过……
It's actually more modern
than mine, I'm ashamed
to admit, but...

27
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:35,933
这是一辆奥迪80，1.8 E。
It's an Audi 80, 1.8 E.

28
00:01:35,967 --> 00:01:38,067
克拉克森：你真花了不到100块？
詹姆斯·梅：千真万确。
CLARKSON: And you paid
less than 100 quid?
JAMES MAY: I did.

29
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:39,133
克拉克森：有路税？
梅：有的。
CLARKSON: Taxed?
MAY: Yes.

30
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:40,533
克拉克森：年检过了？
梅：还剩七个月。
CLARKSON: Tested?
MAY: Seven months.

31
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:42,533
克拉克森：真不敢相信这车只要100镑。
CLARKSON: You really
can't believe that's 100 quid.

32
00:01:42,567 --> 00:01:46,200
亏我还憋着劲准备嘲笑他：
“完蛋！詹姆斯买了间鸡棚回来！”
I mean, I was ready to go,
"Oh, no! James has
bought a hen house!"

33
00:01:46,233 --> 00:01:49,167
话说回来，哈蒙德到底死哪儿去了？
我们的小仓鼠呢？
Anyway, so where's Hammond,
exactly? Where is the Hamster?

34
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:52,700
两人合：他竟然买了辆罗孚！
BOTH: He's bought a Rover!

35
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:53,767
（两人大笑）
(BOTH LAUGH)

36
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,967
天呐！
Oh, God!

37
00:01:55,067 --> 00:01:56,967
梅：老兄，
你买砸了。
MAY: Old man,
you've done it wrong.

38
00:01:57,067 --> 00:01:58,100
看看我车尾标。
Read my back.

39
00:01:58,133 --> 00:01:59,600
理查德·哈蒙德与梅：
“GTI。”
RICHARD HAMMOND AND MAY:
"GTI."

40
00:01:59,633 --> 00:02:01,967
克拉克森：是，我知道，但是……
哈蒙德与梅：16气门！
CLARKSON: Yes, I know but...
HAMMOND AND MAY: 16 valve.

41
00:02:02,067 --> 00:02:04,733
-哈蒙德：好吧，确实，
这窗户降得下去。（轻笑）
-“罗孚”。
-HAMMOND: Yeah, granted
it does go down. (CHUCKLES)
-"Rover."

42
00:02:04,767 --> 00:02:06,267
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

43
00:02:09,867 --> 00:02:13,700
因为我还不确定它漏不漏水，
所以就先这么盖着吧。
Because I'm not sure
if it leaks, so I'm going
to leave that on.

44
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:15,600
-你的收音机呢？
-压根没有。
-Your radio?
-Isn't there.

45
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:18,700
这儿还有不少铁锈，
这儿也是。
There's more rust here
and here.

46
00:02:18,733 --> 00:02:21,500
-行吧，豪车嘛……
-噢，这破烂随时都会掉下来。
-Yeah well, expensive car...
-Oh, that's gonna drop off
any second.

47
00:02:21,533 --> 00:02:23,167
梅：瞧瞧那个。
MAY: Look at that.

48
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:25,100
克拉克森：
好了，我看咱们可以准备
迎接第一项挑战了。
CLARKSON:
Right, I think we're ready
for our first challenge.

49
00:02:25,133 --> 00:02:27,633
-办公室那边来人了。给你。
-哟，信封什么的还挺讲究。
-One of the chaps
from the office. Here it is.
-Ooh, envelope and everything.

50
00:02:27,667 --> 00:02:32,567
“乘火车往返于
伦敦和曼彻斯特之间，
车票需要182英镑。
"The journey from London
to Manchester and back
would cost £182 on the train.

51
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,567
“而你们买车的钱
比这还便宜。
"Your cars cost
less than that.

52
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:37,267
“你们必须沿M1高速向北行驶，
走新修的M6收费公路。
"You must head North on the M1
take the new M6 toll road.

53
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:40,767
“在曼彻斯特的老特拉福德，
曼联主场外集合。
"Rendezvous in Manchester
outside Manchester United
Ground in Old Trafford.

54
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:44,200
“然后再把车开回
Top Gear赛道，
接受你们的下一项挑战。”
"And drive them back
to the Top Gear track
for your next challenge."

55
00:02:44,233 --> 00:02:46,267
-所以就是开到曼彻斯特再开回来。
-小菜一碟。
-So Manchester and back.
-Easy.

56
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,367
-容易得很。
-妥了。
-Easy.
-Okay.

57
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,400
出发！
Let's go!

58
00:02:51,367 --> 00:02:55,667
克拉克森：我们把每辆车
都加满了油，
随即上路。
CLARKSON: We filled
each of them to the brim
with fuel and set off.

59
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,100
不过真挺让人吃惊的，
It is remarkable though

60
00:03:05,133 --> 00:03:07,133
我们居然都能在高速公路的
最外侧超车道上一路狂奔，
that we're all trundling
along the outside lane
of the motorway

61
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:08,733
车速跟其他正常车
不相上下……
same speed
as everybody else...

62
00:03:08,767 --> 00:03:11,600
开的还是花不到
100英镑淘来的破车。
In cars that cost
less than a £100.

63
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:17,733
梅：这辆奥迪简直……
MAY: This Audi is...

64
00:03:17,767 --> 00:03:19,567
呃，无可挑剔，真的。
Well, perfect, really.

65
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:24,467
哈蒙德：当年这台罗孚416 GTI，
说实话，
确实是一坨工业垃圾。
HAMMOND: In its day,
of course, the Rover 416 GTI
was rubbish, really.

66
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,200
方向盘稍微有点歪，
The steering wheel
is not quite on straight,

67
00:03:26,233 --> 00:03:28,233
但这恰好说明
我能把它转手甩卖给黑车司机。
but that just means that
I can flog it to a mini cabber.

68
00:03:31,633 --> 00:03:35,333
我是说，我还以为自己身后
肯定会一路喷着滚滚蓝烟呢。
I mean, I expected to be in
a sort of plume of blue fog.

69
00:03:38,167 --> 00:03:40,333
但到目前为止，它们还挺撑得住。
But they're fine, so far.

70
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,267
克拉克森：
我现在想去撒泡尿。
CLARKSON:
I currently need a pee.

71
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:49,833
不过车里这味儿闻着，
就好像刚刚有人在这儿尿过一样。
（吸鼻子闻）
Smells though, in here,
like other people have just
done it. (SNIFFING)

72
00:03:50,467 --> 00:03:52,200
（吸鼻子闻）
(SNIFFING)

73
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:58,233
我想我现在要把我的
电动阳光大天窗打开了。
I think I'm going to open
my electric sunshine roof now.

74
00:03:59,133 --> 00:04:01,633
让这股清爽的春日空气
吹进来一些。
Let a bit of this crisp
spring air in.

75
00:04:01,667 --> 00:04:03,067
嗯！爽！
Mmm! Nice!

76
00:04:03,067 --> 00:04:05,200
天窗嘛，得，
这茬咱就翻过去不提了。
Sun roof, well,
we'll gloss over that.

77
00:04:05,233 --> 00:04:07,533
我现在真正想要的是一台收音机。
What I do really want
is a radio.

78
00:04:09,233 --> 00:04:13,367
用80年代沃尔沃的车载音响
放罗比·威廉姆斯。
Robbie Williams played through
a 1980's Volvo stereo.

79
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,933
哪怕听广播三台都成啊。
I'd listen to Radio 3.

80
00:04:14,967 --> 00:04:16,933
（车载音响播放着《Angels》）
(ANGEL PLAYING ON STEREO)

81
00:04:16,967 --> 00:04:18,400
或者4台的《阿彻一家》
Or The Arches on 4

82
00:04:18,433 --> 00:04:20,167
♪ 思绪在脑海中翻腾 ♪
# Thoughts running
through my head #

83
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,467
哎，真希望我也有台收音机！
Oh, I wish I had a radio!

84
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:25,833
这是我这辈子听过最烂的音响！
That's the worst stereo
I've ever heard in my life!

85
00:04:25,867 --> 00:04:27,433
哎，真希望我也有台收音机！
Oh, I wish I had a radio!

86
00:04:27,467 --> 00:04:29,633
但这好歹是台立体声音响！
But it's a stereo!

87
00:04:29,667 --> 00:04:31,333
而且哈蒙德连这都没有。
And Hammond doesn't have one.

88
00:04:31,367 --> 00:04:33,233
（哈蒙德在唱歌）
(HAMMOND SINGING)

89
00:04:34,933 --> 00:04:36,600
（胡乱哼唱）
(SCATTING)

90
00:04:38,867 --> 00:04:41,133
法拉利。（嗤笑）
Ferrari. (SCOFFS)

91
00:04:41,167 --> 00:04:44,700
♪ 如果我是个有钱人…… ♪
（乱哼）
# If I were a rich man... #
(SCATTING)

92
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:46,767
（哈蒙德通过扩音喇叭胡乱哼唱）
(HAMMOND SCATTING OVER PA)

93
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:47,567
（大笑）
(LAUGHING)

94
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:50,500
好了，《如果我是个有钱人》唱完了，
还有别的点歌建议吗？
Okay, I've done "If I Were a Rich Man",
any other suggestions?

95
00:04:50,533 --> 00:04:52,533
《如果我是个高个子》？
"If I Were a Tall Man"?

96
00:04:52,567 --> 00:04:55,267
好笑，真好笑。
Funny. Very funny.

97
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:02,400
杰里米自诩为热血车手，
开着他的六缸沃尔沃轰鸣着绝尘而去。
Jeremy being a sporting driver has
roared off in his 6-cylinder Volvo.

98
00:05:02,433 --> 00:05:05,667
你们人呢？我的V6引擎
好像一眨眼就飙没影了。
Where are you? I seem to
have sped off with me V6.

99
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:07,200
但他很快就会后悔的。
But he could regret that.

100
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:12,967
正前方升腾起
一团巨大的浓烟。
There is, coming up ahead,
an enormous cloud of smoke.

101
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,900
我只能推测
那肯定是杰里米了。
Which I can only
assume is Jeremy.

102
00:05:15,933 --> 00:05:18,933
-要是气缸垫冲了，
我们麻烦可就大了。
-梅：那是压缩机。
-If this is a head gasket,
we are in big trouble here.
-MAY: That's the compressor.

103
00:05:18,967 --> 00:05:22,300
克拉克森：事实上，
是带动空调的皮带崩断了，
CLARKSON: In fact,
a belt that drives the air
conditioning had snapped,

104
00:05:22,333 --> 00:05:24,267
还顺带把散热水箱的塞子打飞了。
and knocked a plug
out of the radiator.

105
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:28,667
只要直接把它塞回去，
加满水，我就能重新上路了。
Simply put it back again,
fill that with water
and I was on my way.

106
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:30,400
（众人大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

107
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,700
行了，搞定，
重新上路。
Right, here we go,
back on the road.

108
00:05:35,733 --> 00:05:37,567
杰里米那堆破铜烂铁修好了。
Jeremy's heap of junk fixed.

109
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,633
好得很。
It's fine.

110
00:05:38,667 --> 00:05:39,667
就那台沃尔沃。
That Volvo.

111
00:05:40,767 --> 00:05:42,567
他脑子到底在想什么？
What was he thinking of?

112
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:46,400
好得很，
买来还不到一百镑呢。
It's fine.
It cost less than 100 quid.

113
00:05:55,467 --> 00:05:57,300
克拉克森：
到了，这就是足球场，
CLARKSON:
There we are,
the football stadium

114
00:05:57,333 --> 00:05:59,167
曼彻斯特流浪者队的主场。
where Manchester Rovers play.

115
00:05:59,267 --> 00:06:04,267
现在，该掉头
回演播室了。
And now, it's time to turn
around and head back
to the studio.

116
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:06,267
但这几辆破车能撑得回去吗？
But would the cars make it?

117
00:06:08,667 --> 00:06:10,533
这里是测试赛道。
This is the track.

118
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:15,067
詹姆斯开着他的奥迪过来了。
And here comes James now
in his Audi.

119
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:16,567
它居然挺回来了！
It's back!

120
00:06:17,567 --> 00:06:21,267
理查德也开着他的罗孚回来了。
And so too is Richard,
in the Rover.

121
00:06:23,867 --> 00:06:25,167
小心车漆！
Watch the paintwork!

122
00:06:25,267 --> 00:06:27,033
克拉克森：
但那辆沃尔沃呢？
CLARKSON:
But where's the Volvo?

123
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,433
两人：不会吧！
BOTH: No!

124
00:06:32,467 --> 00:06:35,100
-（梅大笑）
-哈蒙德：我真不敢相信。
-(MAY LAUGHING)
-HAMMOND: I can't believe it.

125
00:06:35,133 --> 00:06:37,000
克拉克森：
没错，你们当初目送它们全部出发。
CLARKSON:
Yes, you counted them all out.

126
00:06:37,033 --> 00:06:39,300
现在你们可以数着
它们全须全尾地开回来了。
And now you can count
them all back again.

127
00:06:39,333 --> 00:06:41,433
事实证明，
今天你随便买辆二手车，
Proof,
today you can buy a car,

128
00:06:41,467 --> 00:06:43,400
哪怕把油钱
也都算在内，
and even including
the cost of fuel,

129
00:06:43,433 --> 00:06:47,800
跑一趟曼彻斯特打个来回，
花的钱也比
坐火车便宜。
go to Manchester
and back for less than
it would cost on the train.

130
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:51,900
而且更绝的是，
要是你坐火车跑完一趟，
And what's more,
if you finish a train journey,

131
00:06:51,933 --> 00:06:53,833
你最后剩下的
就只有一张废车票，
all you're left with
is a used ticket

132
00:06:53,867 --> 00:06:56,533
外加邻座传给你的
一身毛病。
and a disease from the person
who's sitting next to you.

133
00:06:56,567 --> 00:06:58,300
没错，而且坐在你旁边的
Yeah, and the person
you're sitting next to

134
00:06:58,333 --> 00:07:01,267
永远都是同一个喝得烂醉的
格拉斯哥脚手架工。
你们注意过没有？
is always the same drunken
Glaswegian scaffolder.
Have you noticed?

135
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,300
对，还带了整整20箱哈普啤酒。
Yeah, with 20 cases of Harp.

136
00:07:03,333 --> 00:07:04,533
是啊，全让你给喝光了。
Yes, all of which you drink.

137
00:07:04,567 --> 00:07:06,167
反正我们这趟没招惹上脚手架工。
Anyway, we didn't end up
with a scaffolder.

138
00:07:06,267 --> 00:07:10,067
我们最终落到手里的，
是三辆完全能正常上路
跑得好好的破车。
What we ended up with
were three perfectly
serviceable cars.

139
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:13,100
在稍后的节目中，
我们还会对它们
进行更多测试，
And later on in the show,
we are going to be
doing more tests with them

140
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:17,567
来看看它们到底是有多好，
还是有多烂。
to find out just
how good or bad they are.

141
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:21,900
不过现在，进入新闻环节。
我们先来聊聊测速摄像头。
But now though, The News.
And we're starting with speed cameras.

142
00:07:21,933 --> 00:07:26,233
呃，你们懂的，政府死不承认
装那些玩意儿是为了敛财。
Uh, you see, the government denies
that they're there to make money.

143
00:07:26,267 --> 00:07:28,567
（克拉克森和哈蒙德狂笑）
(CLARKSON AND HAMMOND GUFFAW)

144
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:34,800
所以，交通大臣阿利斯泰尔·达林
出台了一项新规。
So, Alistair Darling, the Secretary of
Transport has made a new ruling.

145
00:07:34,833 --> 00:07:41,733
基本上就是说，超速不再扣3分了，
而是改扣2分。
Which is basically, instead of getting
3 points, we're gonna get 2 points.

146
00:07:41,767 --> 00:07:46,767
听着挺合理的嘛。挺公平的！
- 不，完全不是。因为你知道他说什么了吗？
Well that sounds fair enough. Sounds fair!
- No, no. Because do you know what he said?

147
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:54,700
他说在限速30英里的区域，开到30至35扣2分，
要是开到36，直接扣4分！
He says you get 2 points from 30 - 35mph
in a 30 zone, if you're going 36, 4 points!

148
00:07:54,733 --> 00:07:59,400
那扣的分不是更多了吗！对吧。
- 分扣得更多了。扣得更多了！
Well that's more points! Right.
- It's more points. More points!

149
00:07:59,433 --> 00:08:05,633
等等，在旧制度下，你违章4次
才会被吊销驾照禁驾。
Hang on, under the old system, you can do
4 offences before getting banned.

150
00:08:05,667 --> 00:08:09,900
没错。然后你就妻离子散、家破人亡、
工作丢了、孩子也饿死街头。
Exactly. And you lost your wife, your home,
your job, children, starved on the street.

151
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:14,833
但在扣2分的制度下，你能违章6次；
交6次罚款，才会被禁驾。
But under the 2 point system, you get
6 offences; 6 fines and then you're banned.

152
00:08:14,867 --> 00:08:19,300
所以他们能在吊销你驾照之前，
从你身上多榨点油水。是这么回事吧？
So they make more money out of you
before they ban you. Is that right?

153
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:21,833
这就是个骗局。
- 确实，因为虽然每次只扣2分
It is a con.
- That's true, because you'll get 2 points

154
00:08:21,867 --> 00:08:25,067
但罚款照样是60镑……对啊！
他们赚得更多了！
therefore it's £60... yeah!
They make more money!

155
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,800
你还真得佩服他们，
我是说，这招真够阴险狡诈的。
You've kind of got to admire them,
I mean it's crafty.

156
00:08:27,833 --> 00:08:29,967
可不是嘛！咱们有阿利斯泰尔·达林的照片吗？
It is! Have we got a picture
of Alistair Darling?

157
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,400
我觉得大家得瞧瞧这幕后主谋的嘴脸……
快看他！
I think you need to see the brains behind...
look at him!

158
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:38,800
梅：他的头发是夹上去的吧！
- 要么就是眉毛是夹上去的。
MAY: He's got clip-on hair!
- Either that or clip-on eyebrows.

159
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:41,400
其实那根本就是夹上去的一体式假眉毛。
It's actually a clip-on eyebrow.

160
00:08:41,433 --> 00:08:43,300
我跟你们讲，你们去过
当地的超市没有
I tell you what, have you ever been
to your local supermarket

161
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:47,400
还挂着“本月最佳员工”照片？就是他！
and they always have
"Employee of the Month"? It's him!

162
00:08:47,433 --> 00:08:51,967
那家伙居然掌管着全英国的交通！
That man is in charge of
all of Britain's transport!

163
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,233
瞧瞧……（敲电视）
里面啥也没有！完全是空的！
And look... (KNOCKS ON TV)
Nothing in! Completely empty!

164
00:08:56,300 --> 00:09:00,633
脑子空空。好，接下来是一条
相当有意思的意大利警方新闻。
Empty. Right, news from the
Italian police, interestingly enough.

165
00:09:00,667 --> 00:09:05,700
他们搞了辆新警车。
他们本可以选新款菲亚特Panda，
They've got a new police car.
They could've had the new Fiat Panda,

166
00:09:05,733 --> 00:09:09,200
开着多顺手；或者阿尔法·罗密欧156，也挺体面，但并没有。
would've been handy, or an
Alfa 156, nice, but no.

167
00:09:09,233 --> 00:09:13,833
他们搞了辆兰博基尼盖拉多！
瞧瞧这个！
They've got a Lamborghini Gallardo.
Look at this!

168
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:18,900
哈蒙德：这才是真正的警车！
- 没错，但我们纳闷了一整周
HAMMOND: Now THAT is a police car!
- Yes, but we've been wondering all week

169
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:23,933
图啥呢？因为在意大利
你根本不可能构成交通违章。
Why? Because it is impossible to
commit a motoring offence in Italy.

170
00:09:23,967 --> 00:09:26,700
我以前就被意大利警察拦过。
- 为什么？
I've been stopped by the Italian police.
- What for?

171
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:31,733
我当时开着阿斯顿·马丁DB7飙到110英里，超了警车
I was doing about 110 in an
Aston Martin DB7, I overtook the police car

172
00:09:31,767 --> 00:09:36,300
还是在左转弯道上超的，结果他在下一个路旁停车带叫停了我，居然是因为
on a left-hand bend, and he pulled
me up at the next lay-by because

173
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:42,600
我在加油站加完油忘了盖油箱盖。
- 按你的说法，这纯粹是审美问题。
I'd left the filler flap open
in the garage.
- It's a style thing, what you're saying.

174
00:09:42,633 --> 00:09:46,333
破坏了车身线条？
- 他一句话都没说，下了车就……
Spoiling the lines of the car?
- He didn't say anything, just went out...

175
00:09:46,367 --> 00:09:48,367
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

176
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,600
我还以为自己要因为“不够美观”吃罚单了呢。
I thought I was gonna get a ticket
for being unaesthetic.

177
00:09:50,633 --> 00:09:52,633
你当时穿了身上这件衬衫？
- 没……（听不清）
You were wearing that shirt?
- No... (INDISCERNABLE)

178
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:56,300
我们《Top Gear》
其实挺喜欢意大利人的。
- 没错（Si）。
We do, on Top Gear,
rather like the Italians.
- Si.

179
00:09:56,333 --> 00:09:58,033
他们很棒。
（观众赞同）
They are good.
(AUDIENCE IN AGREEMENT)

180
00:09:58,067 --> 00:10:00,067
那边……
- 现场有意大利人吗？
- 咱们这儿有吗？
There's...
- Anybody got one?
- We got some here?

181
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,600
两位意大利老哥？致敬。
Two Italians? Respect.

182
00:10:02,633 --> 00:10:04,533
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

183
00:10:04,567 --> 00:10:07,567
向你们致敬。
- 他俩怎么没坐前排？
Respect to you.
- Why aren't they at the front?

184
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:12,200
因为咱们的警察，伦敦警察
成天开着枣红色的沃克斯豪尔雅特到处巡逻。
'Cause our policemen, London Police
drive around in maroon Vauxhall Astras.

185
00:10:12,233 --> 00:10:16,233
这给游客传递的是什么形象啊？“天呐，英国人穷疯了吧！”
What kind of a message is that giving out
to tourists? "God, they must be broke!"

186
00:10:16,267 --> 00:10:17,467
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

187
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:20,133
人家意大利人虽然真穷，
开的可都是兰博基尼！
The Italians who ARE broke
have got Lamborghinis!

188
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:25,900
大众出新车的消息。
我们很喜欢大众的双门轿跑……你以前开过尚酷（Scirocco）？
News of a new car from VW.
We like their coupés... you had a Scirocco?

189
00:10:25,933 --> 00:10:28,333
开过两辆。
- 我开过尚酷，我们还很喜欢科拉多（Corrado）……
Two.
- I had a Scirocco, we like the Corrado...

190
00:10:28,367 --> 00:10:33,700
行了，又有一款新车要来了。就是这台，
折叠硬顶，长得帅呆了。
Well, there's a new one coming. Here it is,
fabulous looking thing with a folding roof.

191
00:10:33,733 --> 00:10:40,233
售价预计……我们估摸在两万英镑左右。
明年上市，看着真不赖。
It's gonna be... we reckon about £20,000.
On sale next year, that looks fabulous.

192
00:10:40,267 --> 00:10:42,800
2.0升涡轮增压发动机，
基本相当于套了这副漂亮皮囊的高尔夫GTI。
Two litre turbo engine,
kind of a Golf GTI with that body.

193
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:49,200
众所周知，克莱斯勒如今归奔驰所有。
他们搞出了一款新车——300C，
As you know, Chrysler is owned by Mercedes.
They've come up with a new car, the 300C,

194
00:10:49,233 --> 00:10:55,833
底盘用的是上一代奔驰E级，
但换上了纯正的美系车身和发动机。
now it's based on the old E-Class,
but it's got an American body and engine.

195
00:10:55,867 --> 00:11:02,767
一台5.7升V8 Hemi发动机。
- 不错，太棒了。我得承认，尤其是全黑涂装
It's a 5.7 litre V8 Hemi.
- Nice, lovely. I must confess, in black

196
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,700
看起来格外帅气。
particularly, I think that
looks pretty good.

197
00:11:04,733 --> 00:11:07,633
对，看着相当带感。
- 售价多少来着，两万九千九百九十五英镑？
Yeah, that looks fabulous.
- It's gonna be what, £29,995?

198
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:11,567
跟宝马5系一个价。
- 那性价比相当高了，我们觉得。
Same as a 5-Series BMW.
- So that's pretty good, we think.

199
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,900
我很喜欢这外观。
- 挺让人期待的。
I like the look of that.
- Looking forward to that.

200
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:17,900
嗯……只要他们别硬把它调校得太“运动”，
那就差不了。
Well... it'll be good so long as
they don't make it too sporty.

201
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:23,800
怎么了？
- 反正我不喜欢运动轿车。
What?
- Well I don't like sports saloons.

202
00:11:23,833 --> 00:11:28,233
你买辆运动轿车，轮胎就给配得傻大傻大的，
结果操控全完蛋了。
When you get a sports saloon, you get tyres
too big, so the handling goes to pot.

203
00:11:28,267 --> 00:11:31,767
悬挂调得死硬，滤震全毁了，
座椅也硬邦邦的，
The suspension's too firm, so the ride is
spoiled, and the seats are too hard,

204
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:36,400
开上一会儿屁股就疼得不行。
纯粹是把一台好端端的车给糟蹋了。
so you get big bum ache after a while.
It just spoils a perfectly good car.

205
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:41,800
你知道你上的是《Top Gear》，
而不是《赞美之歌》吧？
You are aware this is Top Gear, not
Songs of Praise you're appearing on?

206
00:11:41,833 --> 00:11:43,433
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

207
00:11:43,467 --> 00:11:46,667
其实你提到《赞美之歌》还真挺巧的。
我做了个实验，听着啊。
Actually, it's funny you should mention
Songs of Praise. I did an experiment, okay?

208
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:52,600
连续两周，我每天开车走同一条路线。
第一周，
For two weeks, I did the same journey
every day by car. For the first week,

209
00:11:52,633 --> 00:11:57,633
我决定学你们两个那样，跟裤裆着了火似的狂飙。
而第二周，
I decided to drive like you two, with your
trousers on fire. For the second week,

210
00:11:57,667 --> 00:12:01,667
我就像个虔诚的基督徒车主那样开车，
看看结果到底有什么不同。
I drove like a Christian motorist,
to see if it would make a difference.

211
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:08,500
有意思的来了。第二周，
我到得一样快，有时候甚至更快。
And this is the interesting thing. Week 2,
I got there as quickly, sometimes quicker.

212
00:12:08,533 --> 00:12:11,033
可你怎么像个“基督徒”那样开车？
But how do you drive like
a "Christian" motorist?

213
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:14,300
关键在于宽恕，理查德。
（观众笑声）
It's about forgiveness, Richard.
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

214
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:19,400
打扰一下，不好意思啊詹姆斯，
你指的不就是在岔路口给别人让行嘛。
Can we just, sorry James, you're talking
about letting people out at side turns.

215
00:12:19,433 --> 00:12:21,433
对啊，要是有人想并出来，你就让他并。
Yeah, if somebody wants to
come out, you let them out.

216
00:12:21,467 --> 00:12:24,067
要是看着有人像是要过马路，你就停下。
If somebody looks as if they're going
to step into the road, you stop.

217
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:29,400
然后这样还能让你一样快到家？
And this gets you home just as quickly?

218
00:12:29,433 --> 00:12:30,333
有时候更快。
- 扯淡！
Sometimes quicker.
- Rubbish!

219
00:12:30,367 --> 00:12:33,200
可你要是让别人插进来，你前面不就又多了一辆车！
But if you let somebody out, you've got
another car in front of you!

220
00:12:33,233 --> 00:12:36,167
要是前面有辆车挡着——理查德，你懂这种感觉的——
If I had a car in front of me, and
Richard, you'll identify with this,

221
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:38,600
我就非得把它超过去不可。
- 就是，他们挡了我的道！
I need to be past it.
- Well, they're in my way!

222
00:12:38,633 --> 00:12:42,633
这是头等大事——“你在我前面，我就必须跑到你前面。”
It's the most important thing - "You are in
front of me, I need to be in front."

223
00:12:42,667 --> 00:12:46,867
别挡道，滚一边去！
- 谦卑者必得道路。
Get out of my way, coming through.
- The meek will inherit the road.

224
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,900
放屁！
- 你想开得像迈克尔·舒马赫，
Rubbish!
- You want to drive like Michael Schumacher

225
00:12:48,933 --> 00:12:52,033
但在未来，人们会想像耶稣那样开车。
in the future, people will
want to drive like Jesus.

226
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:57,100
迈克尔·舒马赫可不是靠当基督徒司机
赢下六座世界冠军的。
Michael Schumacher has not won 6 World
Championships by driving like a Christian.

227
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:59,900
不过大卫·库特哈德嘛，倒是有可能……
（观众笑声）
David Coulthard, on the other hand...
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

228
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:04,667
他开车……赛车侧面估计都印着“英国国教会”——
He drives- he's probably got "C of E"
written down the side of his-

229
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:07,667
“您先请！”
- 车屁股上还贴着圣鱼标！
"Come on by!"
- A fish on the back!

230
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:09,700
车屁股贴个小鱼标。
- 不不不不不。
A fish on the back.
- No, no, no, no, no.

231
00:13:09,733 --> 00:13:11,867
不是所有人都懂这个梗。
- 反正我是不懂。
Not everybody gets it.
- Well I don't.

232
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,400
后排已经有观众离场了。
（观众笑声）
There are people at the back leaving.
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

233
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,300
理查德·哈蒙德……？
我换个话题了啊。
Richard Hammond...?
I'm moving on now.

234
00:13:18,867 --> 00:13:21,900
理查德·哈蒙德，
你很喜欢狗，对吧？
Richard Hammond,
you like dogs, don't you?

235
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,233
对，我养了四只，爱得不行。
Yes, I've got four of them.
I love them.

236
00:13:23,267 --> 00:13:25,300
- 其中有一只是贵宾犬。
- 行了行了，知道啦。
-One of which is a poodle.
-Yes, all right.

237
00:13:25,333 --> 00:13:27,233
- 我只是想让大家心里有数。
- 就只有一只好吧。
-Just wanted them to know.
-Only one of them.

238
00:13:27,267 --> 00:13:29,433
正因如此，
理查德受邀……
And as a result,
Richard was asked to,

239
00:13:29,467 --> 00:13:32,467
在咱们冬季停播期间，
去主持克鲁弗兹犬展。
while we were off air
for the winter,
to host Crufts .

240
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:33,833
没错。
Yes.

241
00:13:33,867 --> 00:13:36,733
显而易见，在这过程中
他丢尽了脸面。
Obviously, he lost a lot
of dignity in the process.

242
00:13:36,767 --> 00:13:42,967
所以他现在决定买辆新车，
好把丢掉的尊严给挣回来。
So now he's decided to
put some of that dignity back
by buying himself a new car.

243
00:13:42,967 --> 00:13:44,967
（引擎轰鸣声）
(ENGINE ROARING)

244
00:13:49,967 --> 00:13:52,967
来看看入围选手，
道奇Charger。
Meet the shortlist,
the Dodge Charger.

245
00:13:52,967 --> 00:13:56,000
哈蒙德：
对我而言，它就是有史以来
最伟大的美国车。
HAMMOND:
For me, the greatest
American car ever.

246
00:14:04,967 --> 00:14:10,767
今天对我来说是个大日子，
因为这是我生平第一次
开道奇Charger。
This is a big day for me,
because it's my first ever
drive in a Dodge Charger.

247
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:12,400
而且我还真有点紧张。
And I'm a little bit nervous.

248
00:14:12,433 --> 00:14:14,967
哈蒙德：
要知道，这车我惦记了一辈子。
HAMMOND:
You see, I've wanted
one of these forever.

249
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,467
可万一它烂透了呢？
But what if it's rubbish?

250
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:19,133
万一真应了那句
