00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,467
我们都知道那场追车戏，对吧？
we all know that
car chase scene, yes?

384
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:11,333
仔细看结尾。
Look very carefully
at the end.

385
00:21:11,367 --> 00:21:14,233
导演当时对
开Charger的资深特技车手说，
The director said to
a highly trained stunt driver
in the Charger,

386
00:21:14,267 --> 00:21:17,800
“我要你直接撞进那个车库，
然后车库就会爆炸。”
"I want you to drive
into that garage,
it will then blow up."

387
00:21:17,833 --> 00:21:19,700
-结果他根本没撞中车库！
-对，他跑偏了。
-He missed the garage!
-Yeah, he did.

388
00:21:19,733 --> 00:21:22,300
仔细看的话，你能看到他
呼啸着从旁边擦了过去。
If you look, you can see him
screaming by.

389
00:21:22,333 --> 00:21:24,867
坦白讲，换作某些人
甚至会把这当成
一项安全配置呢。
And some people
might call that a safety
feature, frankly.

390
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:29,167
要是你那哥们儿当年开的不是那台，
而是开眼前这台Charger，
And if your guy had not
been in that and had
been in one of these,

391
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:31,933
他最后肯定也能完美避开推土机，
捡回一条小命！
he would have missed
those bulldozers in the end
and survived!

392
00:21:31,967 --> 00:21:34,433
所以哪台车
长得更好看？
Which is the better
looking car?

393
00:21:34,467 --> 00:21:36,400
觉得是Charger的，举手。
The Charger, hands up.

394
00:21:37,933 --> 00:21:39,733
Challenger呢？
Challenger?

395
00:21:39,767 --> 00:21:41,167
哈，那显然是Charger赢了。
Ah, it's the Charger then,
clearly.

396
00:21:41,167 --> 00:21:42,967
还有，
关于电影我没说错吧？
And also,
am I right on the film?

397
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,667
有人能想出
比《粉身碎骨》更棒的追车电影吗？
Can anybody think
of a better car chase film
than Vanishing Point?

398
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:49,267
什么？你在哪呢？
等会儿，看这边。
What? Where are you?
Hold on a minute, over here.

399
00:21:49,300 --> 00:21:51,433
-《碟中谍》？
-阿汤哥演的那个。
-Mission Impossible?
-With Tom Cruise.

400
00:21:51,467 --> 00:21:53,900
保时捷大战奥迪TT。
简直太精彩了。
Porsche and Audi TT.
Fantastic.

401
00:21:53,933 --> 00:21:55,233
而且还有个漂亮姑娘。
And a beautiful woman as well.

402
00:21:55,267 --> 00:21:58,267
不，你看，
这简直是我这辈子听过...
No, you see,
that's the biggest load
of dribble...

403
00:21:58,300 --> 00:21:59,700
（众人大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

404
00:21:59,733 --> 00:22:01,067
最扯淡的胡说八道。
I've ever heard in my life.

405
00:22:01,167 --> 00:22:04,033
因为他在那儿原地打转的时候？
Because when he does that
spinning round thing?

406
00:22:04,067 --> 00:22:05,700
-对啊。
-你觉得那能看？
-Yeah.
-You think that's believable?

407
00:22:05,733 --> 00:22:07,633
好吧，行吧。
Well, okay.

408
00:22:07,667 --> 00:22:09,333
真见鬼！纯属白日梦。
Damn it! La la land.

409
00:22:09,367 --> 00:22:12,000
-哈蒙德：别认怂啊...
-我是不是听到有人提《浪人》了？
-HAMMOND: Don't back down...
-Did I hear somebody
say Ronin?

410
00:22:12,033 --> 00:22:13,367
观众：对。
哈蒙德：那片子不错。
MAN: Yes.
HAMMOND: Good film.

411
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:15,000
-还记得《浪人》吗？
-奥迪S8。
-Remember Ronin?
-Audi S8.

412
00:22:15,033 --> 00:22:16,733
奥迪S8... 你干嘛
不买一辆奥迪S8呢？
Audi S8... Why don't
you buy an Audi S8?

413
00:22:16,767 --> 00:22:19,200
奥迪的转向好多了，
正好能一头撞进车库。
Audi's got a better steering,
it would hit the garage.

414
00:22:19,233 --> 00:22:21,533
-还有人要说吗？
-（众人大笑）
-Anyone else?
-(ALL LAUGHING)

415
00:22:21,567 --> 00:22:24,067
-《福禄双霸天》。
-《福禄双霸天》？
啊，快得了吧！
-Blues Brothers.
-Blues Brothers?
Ah, get out!

416
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:27,200
所以说到底就是这样。
So really there we are.

417
00:22:27,233 --> 00:22:30,767
我们已经成功得出结论，
《粉身碎骨》
是有史以来最棒的赛车电影。
We've managed to establish
that Vanishing Point
is the best car film ever.

418
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:33,167
-（笑）才没有！
-就有！
全场人都问遍了！
-(LAUGHING) We haven't!
-We have!
We've been around the room!

419
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,900
我很理解这种
跟着电影买车的毛病。
I understand this,
buying from films.

420
00:22:34,933 --> 00:22:36,867
但事实是，
我们已经达成共识了，
But the fact of the matter is,
we've established

421
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:39,000
《粉身碎骨》，
史上最伟大的汽车电影。
Vanishing Point,
greatest car film ever.

422
00:22:39,033 --> 00:22:40,600
那车是挑战者（Challenger）。
你买错车了。
That's the Challenger.
You're buying the wrong car.

423
00:22:40,633 --> 00:22:42,333
行了吧，你们才没达成共识，
你们全错了。
Okay, you haven't established
that, you're all wrong.

424
00:22:42,367 --> 00:22:45,367
我就要战马（Charger）。
少废话。
我就要这一台。
I want the Charger.
That's that.
That's what I'm having.

425
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:47,800
话说哈蒙德，
这车成色好的要多少钱？
Now, Hammond, how much
is a good one of these?

426
00:22:47,833 --> 00:22:50,000
呃，客观来说，
大概18,000英镑。
Um, about £18,000,
realistically.

427
00:22:50,033 --> 00:22:51,300
18,000镑？好啊。
£18,000? Right.

428
00:22:51,333 --> 00:22:54,700
那这就意味着，
你得把这台车给卖了。
So that means, you're gonna
have to sell this.

429
00:22:54,733 --> 00:22:56,367
-我的心头肉啊。
-没错。
-My pride and joy.
-Yeah.

430
00:22:56,400 --> 00:23:01,533
就是你那台开了22年的
左舵
保时捷911 G系列。
It's your 22-year-old,
left hand drive,
Porsche 911 G Series.

431
00:23:01,567 --> 00:23:02,867
多漂亮啊。
Lovely.

432
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:04,200
你觉得这车
能卖多少钱？
How much do you think
you're gonna get for this?

433
00:23:04,233 --> 00:23:06,467
-大约八千镑吧。
-（坏笑）
-About eight grand.
-(SMIRKS)

434
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:08,333
-啥？
-（众人大笑）
-What?
-(ALL LAUGHING)

435
00:23:08,367 --> 00:23:10,467
8,000镑？
£8,000?

436
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:12,533
这车远比这值钱好吗！
They're worth much more!

437
00:23:12,567 --> 00:23:14,000
-什么？
-乐观估计...
-What?
-Optimistically...

438
00:23:14,033 --> 00:23:16,500
你还差整整一万镑。
要我说，很可能差得更多。
You are 10 grand short.
Probably more, I would say.

439
00:23:16,533 --> 00:23:19,500
-你得去多给几家超市剪彩了。
-没错。
-You're gonna have to
open some supermarkets.
-Yeah.

440
00:23:19,533 --> 00:23:22,400
也许电视机前的观众
能在这事上拉他一把。
Maybe the viewers
can help him on that.

441
00:23:22,433 --> 00:23:25,400
要是你有什么新店
需要剪彩开张，
If you've got a shop
that needs opening,

442
00:23:25,433 --> 00:23:28,333
或者打扫卫生，又或者需要
有人帮忙摆货架。
or cleaning or if you need
any of the shelf stacking.

443
00:23:28,367 --> 00:23:29,667
只限最底下那层……
Just the bottom shelves...

444
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:31,267
对，只限最底下那层，
上面的可够不着。
Yeah, just the bottom shelves,
not the top ones.

445
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:32,800
-（全场大笑）
-克拉克森：底下的他够得着。
-(ALL LAUGHING)
-CLARKSON: He'll reach those.

446
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:35,333
不妨写信给我们，
地址是，呃……
Why don't you write
to us at, um...

447
00:23:35,367 --> 00:23:36,900
（克拉克森读信箱地址）
(CLARKSON READING)

448
00:23:44,833 --> 00:23:46,900
或者也可以上网找我们，
网址是……
Or we could be found
on the internet at...

449
00:23:46,933 --> 00:23:48,633
（读网址）
(READING)

450
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:52,267
多谢两位帮忙啊，
我可太感激了。
Thanks for your help guys,
I appreciate that.

451
00:23:52,300 --> 00:23:55,467
客气啥。不过现在，
是时候见见我们的嘉宾了。
No problem. It's time now,
though, to meet our guest.

452
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:57,733
自从她走出热带丛林，
Ever since she came
out of the jungle,

453
00:23:57,767 --> 00:24:00,700
就成了一位
货真价实的超级巨星。
she has become
a bonafide superstar.

454
00:24:00,733 --> 00:24:01,933
可谓家喻户晓。
She's a household name.

455
00:24:01,967 --> 00:24:04,367
富得超出
最贪婪之人的想象。
She's rich beyond
the dreams of avarice.

456
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:06,433
她还写了本自传。
She's written
an autobiography.

457
00:24:06,467 --> 00:24:11,067
而据我所知，
她其实什么正经事都没干过。
And as far as I can work out
she's done absolutely nothing.

458
00:24:11,833 --> 00:24:13,933
女士们，先生们，乔丹！
Ladies and gentleman, Jordan.

459
00:24:13,967 --> 00:24:15,933
（观众鼓掌）
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

460
00:24:19,033 --> 00:24:20,500
-嗨。
-你好啊。
-Hiya.
-How are you?

461
00:24:23,800 --> 00:24:25,167
请坐。
Have a seat.

462
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:31,400
你的自传，
畅销书排行榜第一名。
Your autobiography,
number one,
in the bestseller list.

463
00:24:31,433 --> 00:24:35,033
我知道。还不错吧，
对我这样的人来说挺不错了，我想。
I know. Not bad,
not bad for someone like me,
I suppose.

464
00:24:35,067 --> 00:24:37,567
太棒了，
而且读起来挺有意思的。
It's fantastic
and it's a good read.

465
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:39,067
这么说你读过了？
You've read it then?

466
00:24:39,167 --> 00:24:40,433
-读了，
我当然读过了。
-你居然真读了？
-I have.
Of course I've read it.
-You've actually read it?

467
00:24:40,467 --> 00:24:41,700
考考我啊。
Test me.

468
00:24:41,733 --> 00:24:43,567
呃，算了，
我待会儿再考你。
Um, no, I'll ask
you after, actually.

469
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:46,867
尽管考，上周末我躺在花园里，
阳光明媚！
You can do, 'cause I lay
in the garden last weekend,
beautiful sunshine!

470
00:24:46,900 --> 00:24:49,167
往那一躺，一个半小时，
全看进去了。
Lay there, hour and half.
I absorbed it all.

471
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:51,100
好吧，确实通俗易懂。
- 确实一点不费脑子。
Well, it's an easy read.
- It is an easy read.

472
00:24:51,133 --> 00:24:55,633
我想跟你聊一件事，
如果可以的话，显然这些年跟你关系
One thing I just want to talk to you about,
if I may, obviously one of the guys you've

473
00:24:55,667 --> 00:24:59,667
很亲近的人里有拉尔夫·舒马赫，
瞧，就是这位：
become friendly over the years is
Ralf Schumacher, here he is:

474
00:25:00,700 --> 00:25:05,300
你在书里形容他
“长相帅气”。
- 呃，这张照片拍得太丑了。
You describe him in your book as
"good looking."
- Well, it's a bad picture.

475
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:07,800
这已经是挑的最好的一张了！
（观众大笑）
That's the best!
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

476
00:25:09,300 --> 00:25:16,200
他究竟哪里吸引你了？
- 呃，隔着桌子时的眼神交流。
What was it that attracted you to him?
- Um, the eye contact across the table.

477
00:25:16,233 --> 00:25:18,233
（清嗓子）
而且这关系持续了大概三年。
(CLEARS THROAT)
And it went on for about 3 years.

478
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:19,267
真的？
- 真的。
Really?
- Yeah.

479
00:25:19,300 --> 00:25:24,400
你看，关键是你在德国跟他待过一阵子，
还有蒙特卡洛，
You see, the thing is you spend some time
with him in Germany, and Monte Carlo,

480
00:25:24,433 --> 00:25:28,300
我记得是，后来还在迈阿密待过，
你们睡过了？
I think, and then some time with him in
Miami, you slept together?

481
00:25:28,333 --> 00:25:31,833
（听不清）
不不，信我，还有的是猛料呢。
(UNINTELLIGIBLE)
No, no, there's plenty more, believe me.

482
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:36,500
你跟他睡过挺多次的。
- 额哼，但我们连一档都没挂上。
You slept with him a lot of times.
- Uh huh. We didn't go into first gear.

483
00:25:36,533 --> 00:25:38,533
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

484
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:43,800
什么都没发生？
- 没呢。好吧，就接了个吻，摸了把胸，
Nothing happened?
- No. Well, a kiss and a ".." on the boob,

485
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:45,833
仅此而已。
（观众笑声）
that was it.
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

486
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:50,400
不过你确实管他叫“千万富翁”，
这当然算是个加分项。
You do refer to him as a "multimillionaire"
though, which is of course a plus side.

487
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:52,800
而且他也确实挺照顾你的。
- 不过我现在自己有钱了。
And he did look after you.
- Now I got my own money though.

488
00:25:52,833 --> 00:25:54,167
身边根本不需要男人。
So I don't need a man there.

489
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,733
没毛病，你现在混得风生水起。
- 嗯哼。
Exactly, you are doing well.
-Mmm-hmm.

490
00:25:55,767 --> 00:25:58,333
而据我推测，
你赚的这些钱，
全砸在车上了。
And you've spent it,
as far as I can work out,
on cars.

491
00:25:58,367 --> 00:25:59,733
我确实超爱我的车。
I do love my cars.

492
00:25:59,767 --> 00:26:01,167
行，我首先想跟你聊的是，
Well, the first thing I want
to talk to you about is,

493
00:26:01,167 --> 00:26:03,533
你把路虎揽胜
换成卡宴了？
you've swapped a Range Rover
for a Cayenne?

494
00:26:03,567 --> 00:26:06,333
嗯，那辆揽胜我差不多
开了五六年了。
Well I have had
the Range Rover for like,
five, six years now.

495
00:26:06,367 --> 00:26:08,667
你也知道那是好车，
真的，没它我都不知道该怎么过了。
You know they are lovely cars,
you know, I couldn't
go on without them.

496
00:26:08,700 --> 00:26:11,700
后来保时捷那款一上市，
我心想：“真丑，丑死了。”
And then I saw the Porsche
when it come out and
I thought, "Ugly, ugly car."

497
00:26:11,733 --> 00:26:13,933
但后来好多人都说
这车跑得挺快的。
But then a lot of people said
that they're quite fast.

498
00:26:13,967 --> 00:26:17,367
我就琢磨着：
“行吧，那我试试看”，虽说
里面空间看着小了点，
And I thought,
"Okay, I'll try one", although
they looked smaller inside,

499
00:26:17,400 --> 00:26:21,200
但我发现它
快得多，而且
抓地性能也更好。
I find they're
a lot faster and they do
hold the road better.

500
00:26:21,233 --> 00:26:23,167
- 是Turbo还是S？
- Turbo。
-It is a Turbo or an S?
-Turbo.

501
00:26:23,200 --> 00:26:25,600
- 你买了辆卡宴Turbo？
- 嗯。
-You've got Cayenne Turbo?
-Mmm.

502
00:26:25,633 --> 00:26:27,433
开着感觉怎样？是不是……
How's it going? Is it...

503
00:26:27,467 --> 00:26:30,467
哎，按我平时的开车风格，
你刚才没看到我在赛道上吗？我就是可劲造。
Well, the way I drive cars,
didn't you see me
out there? I trash 'em.

504
00:26:30,500 --> 00:26:32,967
四轮定位绝对跑偏了，
八成是我老蹭马路牙子给磕的。
The tracking's definitely
gone, probably why
I keep kerbing it.

505
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:34,700
噢，懂了……
Oh, I see...

506
00:26:34,733 --> 00:26:36,567
我是说蹭马路牙子，
车轮上路肩的那种，可不是指那种……
I mean kerbing it,
it's on the kerb,
it's not kerbing as in...

507
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:38,033
你的意思是你没去“路边招嫖拉客”。
You don't go kerb crawling,
is what you're saying.

508
00:26:38,067 --> 00:26:39,967
- 没，我觉得我根本不需要。
- 你何必呢？
-No, I don't think I need to.
-Why would you?

509
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,567
（笑声）
(LAUGHS)

510
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,867
不过你现在左右为难的是，
你有一辆宾利Azure，对吧？
But your dilemma is,
you've got this
Bentley Azure, yes?

511
00:26:43,900 --> 00:26:46,967
相当帅气的车。你看，
这儿还有张你坐在里面的照片。
It's quite, quite cool. You see, look,
there's a picture of you in it.

512
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:50,733
虽说显而易见不是真拍的，是我们
顺手用Photoshop把你P上去的。
I think, well it isn't obviously, we've put
you in there in a sort-of Photoshop way.

513
00:26:51,200 --> 00:26:53,067
不过呃，你的备选方案是什么？
But um, what's your alternative?

514
00:26:53,100 --> 00:26:54,533
你打算买哪辆来换它？
What you thinking
of getting instead?

515
