654
00:32:31,233 --> 00:32:34,500
而且它简直气势磅礴。
瞧瞧这大块头！
And it is magnificent.
Just look at the size of it!

655
00:32:34,533 --> 00:32:39,300
劳斯莱斯原话说，
它跑起来的样子
理应像一艘破浪前行的奢华快艇。
Rolls-Royce actually say
it's supposed to look like
a posh motorboat in motion.

656
00:32:39,333 --> 00:32:43,933
还真有那么点意思。
瞧这儿，车尾甚至还铺了柚木甲板。
And it kind of does.
It's even got teak decking,
here at the back.

657
00:32:43,967 --> 00:32:49,233
一位来自“德意志祖国”的大汉
穿着宝马T恤，把车送到了我们手上。
A man from the Vaterland
delivered the car to us,
in a BMW T-shirt.

658
00:32:49,267 --> 00:32:51,067
而且他神情极其严肃，对我说……
And he was very strict,
he said to me...

659
00:32:51,067 --> 00:32:52,967
（讲德语）
(SPEAKING GERMAN)

660
00:32:53,067 --> 00:32:56,133
“因为这是由一整块铝合金精密加工而成的。”
Because it's made of a single
piece of machined aluminium.

661
00:32:56,167 --> 00:32:58,367
不过这个呢，却是……
This though is...

662
00:32:58,400 --> 00:33:00,267
纯银打造的。
Solid silver.

663
00:33:00,300 --> 00:33:01,833
厉害吧？
不过我真正喜欢的……
How about that?
But what I really like...

664
00:33:01,867 --> 00:33:03,233
我对这辆车真正中意的是……
What I really like
about this is...

665
00:33:03,267 --> 00:33:06,533
通常这玩意儿上配的那台娘炮V12，
The normal nancy-boy V12
that you get in these things

666
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:09,067
被换成了一台V16发动机，
has been replaced
by a V16 engine

667
00:33:09,067 --> 00:33:13,267
而它的存在纯粹是为了极致平顺。
我就好这一口，太对我胃口了。
and it's there purely
for smoothness.
I like that. I like this.

668
00:33:13,300 --> 00:33:17,333
劳斯莱斯放话说绝不会量产这台车。
Rolls-Royce has said
they'll never build this car.

669
00:33:17,367 --> 00:33:21,500
所以大家就等着它很快上市吧，
售价大概三十万英镑。
So expect to see it
on sale soon
for about £300,000.

670
00:33:22,733 --> 00:33:25,167
好了，刚才我们仨已经证明了，
Okay, now earlier on
the three of us proved

671
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:28,967
我们那几台100英镑淘来的破车真能跑去曼彻斯特再开回来。
that our £100 cars could make
it to Manchester and back.

672
00:33:29,067 --> 00:33:30,767
但现在它们来到了赛道，
But now they're at the track,

673
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:33,367
节目摄制组精心策划了一系列的测试，
and the production team
have come up with
a number of tests

674
00:33:33,400 --> 00:33:35,133
来看看它们到底还剩几分能耐，
to find out how
functional they are,

675
00:33:35,167 --> 00:33:37,800
跑得有多快，
而最最关键的是，到底有多安全。
how fast they are,
and most of all
how safe they are.

676
00:33:37,833 --> 00:33:40,600
而且说实话，也顺便看看，
And as a kind
of by-product, really,

677
00:33:40,633 --> 00:33:42,900
我们三个里谁捡的便宜最大。
which one of us
got the best deal.

678
00:33:45,867 --> 00:33:47,900
克拉克森：
这就是我们买的几台车。
CLARKSON:
Here are the cars we bought.

679
00:33:47,933 --> 00:33:54,400
理查德的罗孚GTI，
詹姆斯的奥迪80，
还有我的V6沃尔沃GLE。
There's Richard's Rover GTI,
James's Audi 80,
and my V6 Volvo GLE.

680
00:33:54,433 --> 00:33:56,500
下面是第一项测试。
And here's the first test.

681
00:33:56,533 --> 00:34:00,267
后台工作人员算出了
我们在曼彻斯特那趟行程中
消耗了多少燃油。
Our researchers worked out
how much fuel was used
on the Manchester run.

682
00:34:00,300 --> 00:34:04,700
目标油耗是30英里每加仑，
每高出1个mpg，
就能得1分。
30 mpg was the target
for every mile to the gallon,
over that you get a point.

683
00:34:04,733 --> 00:34:08,633
每低于1个mpg，
就扣1分。
For every mpg under it,
you lose a point.

684
00:34:08,667 --> 00:34:10,067
（听不清）
(INAUDIBLE)

685
00:34:11,367 --> 00:34:14,667
好，我拿到油耗测试的
成绩单了。
Right, I have the results
of the economy run.

686
00:34:14,700 --> 00:34:21,733
沃尔沃，油耗20英里每加仑，
杰里米喜提
负10分。
The Volvo, 20 miles
to the gallon, giving Jeremy
a score of minus 10.

687
00:34:21,767 --> 00:34:24,100
罗孚，
23英里每加仑，
The Rover,
23 miles to the gallon,

688
00:34:24,133 --> 00:34:26,667
让理查德拿到了
负7分。
giving Richard a score
of minus seven.

689
00:34:26,700 --> 00:34:31,300
至于奥迪呢？
令人惊叹的
35英里每加仑，
And the Audi?
A remarkable 35
miles to the gallon,

690
00:34:31,333 --> 00:34:33,700
我喜获5分。
giving me five points.

691
00:34:33,733 --> 00:34:38,500
没错。不过我刚被告知，
我们还要接受
可靠性测试。
Yes. Now I have just been
told that we're also going
to be tested on reliability.

692
00:34:38,533 --> 00:34:41,333
引擎盖每掀开一次，
就得扣1分。
We're gonna lose a point
for every time the bonnet
had to be lifted.

693
00:34:41,367 --> 00:34:44,200
也就是说，
詹姆斯你一分没扣。
Which means,
none there for you, James.

694
00:34:44,233 --> 00:34:48,800
我也没扣。
但杰里米还得再扣1分。
None for me.
And minus another one
for Jeremy.

695
00:34:48,833 --> 00:34:51,233
行吧，我承认，
我的沃尔沃表现确实不太行。
Okay, I admit it.
My Volvo's not doing well.

696
00:34:51,267 --> 00:34:55,700
不过现在该进行
下一项挑战了，
规则是……
But it's time now
for the next challenge,
which is...

697
00:34:55,733 --> 00:34:59,067
“每辆车都要在赛道上
刷一圈最快圈速，
"Each car will complete
one fast lap of the track

698
00:34:59,100 --> 00:35:01,767
“由一位独立裁判
亲自掌舵。
"in the hands of an
independent adjudicator.

699
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:04,333
“目标时间是
1分50秒。
"One minute fifty seconds
is the target.

700
00:35:04,367 --> 00:35:06,400
“每比目标时间快1秒，
得1分。
"For every second
you go faster than that
you get a point.

701
00:35:06,433 --> 00:35:09,967
“每慢1秒，
扣1分。”
"For every second slower,
you lose a point."

702
00:35:10,067 --> 00:35:13,100
不知道这位“独立裁判”
会是何方神圣呢？
I wonder who the independent
adjudicator might be?

703
00:35:14,867 --> 00:35:17,633
克拉克森：
首先出场的是理查德的GTI。
CLARKSON:
First to go is Richard's GTI.

704
00:35:17,667 --> 00:35:19,167
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

705
00:35:21,967 --> 00:35:24,600
这大概是斯提格开过
最烂的一辆车了。
This is probably the worst car
the Stig has ever driven.

706
00:35:24,633 --> 00:35:27,867
不过平心而论，
可能还算不上他今天
要开的最烂的一辆。
Although, it must be said,
probably not the worst car
he's going to drive today.

707
00:35:27,900 --> 00:35:29,067
两人：那确实不是。
BOTH: No.

708
00:35:32,067 --> 00:35:34,633
好了，他现在正杀向
双髻鲨弯（Hammerhead）。
Okay, he's going down now
towards the Hammerhead.

709
00:35:34,667 --> 00:35:36,400
时速大概飙到四五十英里了吧？
He's probably up to 40 or 50?

710
00:35:36,433 --> 00:35:37,600
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECH)

711
00:35:41,733 --> 00:35:43,067
他正准备切入
贯通弯（Follow Through）。
He's coming through
to the Follow Through.

712
00:35:43,067 --> 00:35:45,067
我敢打赌他绝对得松油门。
Now my bet is he'll lift.

713
00:35:47,767 --> 00:35:50,667
哇噢！他居然还活着！
Whoa! He's still alive!

714
00:35:50,700 --> 00:35:52,133
（众人大笑）
(ALL LAUGH)

715
00:35:53,533 --> 00:35:56,867
克拉克森：现在来看看
詹姆斯的奥迪表现如何。
CLARKSON: Now let's see
how James's Audi goes.

716
00:35:59,733 --> 00:36:02,100
刚才这0到60英里加速
大概用了25分钟吧。
That was 0 to 60
in about 25 minutes.

717
00:36:02,133 --> 00:36:03,967
哈蒙德：
前提是它真能开到60英里。
HAMMOND:
Assuming it will ever
get to 60.

718
00:36:04,067 --> 00:36:07,200
梅：现在就能看出
选装运动套件的
巨大优势了。
MAY: This is where we will see
the advantage of the optional
sport pack.

719
00:36:07,233 --> 00:36:08,400
（众人哄笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

720
00:36:11,933 --> 00:36:13,133
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECH)

721
00:36:15,300 --> 00:36:18,867
克拉克森：斯提格跑完后说，
他觉得这辆奥迪以前
肯定遭遇过严重事故，
CLARKSON: The Stig said after
this run, he thought the Audi
had been in a big accident

722
00:36:18,900 --> 00:36:22,733
而且修得根本不到位。
at some point in its life,
and not mended properly.

723
00:36:22,767 --> 00:36:25,567
但他对我那辆沃尔沃的评价更刻薄。
But he was even ruder
about my Volvo.

724
00:36:29,467 --> 00:36:33,767
哈蒙德：
（大笑）问题是，
它就是死活甩不掉啊！
HAMMOND:
(LAUGHING) The thing is,
he's just not going away!

725
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:35,567
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGH)

726
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:37,200
它还在后头跟着呢！
It's still there!

727
00:36:41,233 --> 00:36:44,533
一百七十匹制动马力！
One hundred and seventy
brake horsepower!

728
00:36:44,567 --> 00:36:48,900
两人合：是啊，但车重也足足有一百七十吨！
BOTH: Yeah, but 170 tonnes
of the car to boot!

729
00:36:48,933 --> 00:36:50,100
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGH)

730
00:36:57,533 --> 00:36:59,300
那么成绩揭晓……
So the results...

731
00:36:59,333 --> 00:37:02,767
理查德的罗孚跑了一分四十二秒。
Richard's Rover went round
in one min forty two seconds.

732
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:06,800
比一分五十秒的目标
快了足足八秒。
So, that is eight seconds
under the one minute
fifty target.

733
00:37:06,833 --> 00:37:09,267
这就意味着拿到八分。
That means eight points.

734
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:13,500
詹姆斯的奥迪比目标快了四秒，一分四十六。
James's Audi was four seconds
under the target, a 1.46.

735
00:37:13,533 --> 00:37:16,133
所以他拿到四分。
So he gets four points.

736
00:37:16,167 --> 00:37:19,967
还有我的沃尔沃，一分四十八，拿了两分。
And my Volvo, 1.48.
So that's two points.

737
00:37:20,067 --> 00:37:22,367
加分了！好歹是正分！
It's a plus! It's a plus!

738
00:37:22,400 --> 00:37:25,467
行，下一项测试。
把任务信封给我好吗？谢谢。
Okay, another test.
So if I could have
the envelope? Thank you.

739
00:37:25,500 --> 00:37:28,867
“《公路法规》写道：
‘在时速六十英里下，
"The Highway Code says,
'The stopping distance
from 60 miles an hour

740
00:37:28,900 --> 00:37:31,800
不计反应时间的刹车距离为六十码。’”
"'is 60 yards,
without thinking time.'"

741
00:37:31,833 --> 00:37:33,700
不过我们根本用不着管那个。
But we don't need any of that.

742
00:37:33,733 --> 00:37:37,767
“你的车停稳时每比这个距离短一码，
就能得一分。”
"You'll get one point
for every yard less than
that your car pulls up in."

743
00:37:38,300 --> 00:37:42,500
这就是我们必须踩刹车的标线。而在六十码开外，立着一面
This is the line where we have to brake.
And 60 yards away, there's a sort of

744
00:37:42,533 --> 00:37:49,333
“车界公敌”肖像墙：约翰·普雷斯科特、理查德·布伦斯特罗姆，还有一台测速照相机。
"motoring rogues" gallery. John Prescott,
Richard Brunstrom, and a speed camera.

745
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:55,500
哈蒙德：
詹姆斯上了，正在以时速六十英里全力刹车。
HAMMOND:
Here's James, braking
from 60 miles an hour.

746
00:37:55,533 --> 00:37:57,233
来了！
Here we go.

747
00:37:57,267 --> 00:37:59,433
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECH)

748
00:37:59,467 --> 00:38:01,833
噢，又稳又直！
Oh, straight and true!

749
00:38:01,867 --> 00:38:03,300
梅：有种超我啊，哈蒙德。
MAY: Beat that, Hammond.

750
00:38:03,333 --> 00:38:06,633
好，时速到六十了，
只要刹得比詹姆斯短就行。
走着！
Okay, I'm at 60,
just James to beat.
Here we go.

751
00:38:06,667 --> 00:38:09,467
刹车！没反应？！
Braking! Nothing!

752
00:38:09,500 --> 00:38:10,967
（轮胎惨叫声）
(TYRES SQUEALING)

753
00:38:12,567 --> 00:38:13,933
（闷哼）
(GRUNTS)

754
00:38:14,633 --> 00:38:16,667
（大口喘气）
(PANTS)

755
00:38:16,700 --> 00:38:18,400
遗憾的是，我没能赢过詹姆斯。
Sadly, I couldn't beat James.

756
00:38:18,433 --> 00:38:22,167
但杰里米那台大胖子沃尔沃肯定得掉链子。
But surely that fat Volvo
would let Jeremy down.

757
00:38:25,367 --> 00:38:26,967
防抱死刹车！
Anti-lock brakes!

758
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:30,567
漂亮！太棒了！
沃尔沃拿分了！
Yes! Yes! Yes!
The Volvo scored a point!

759
00:38:34,500 --> 00:38:36,267
多好的车啊！
What a great car!

760
00:38:36,300 --> 00:38:37,800
好。刹车……
Right. Brakes.

761
00:38:37,833 --> 00:38:41,333
话说，
詹姆斯的奥迪刹停距离
是40码，
Now then,
James's Audi pulled up
in 40 yards,

762
00:38:41,367 --> 00:38:43,900
比《公路法规》规定的
刹车距离少了20码，
which is 20 under
the Highway Code's
stopping distance,

763
00:38:43,933 --> 00:38:47,700
这意味着，
他拿到了20分。
which means,
he gets 20 points.

764
00:38:47,733 --> 00:38:53,300
接着我的罗孚停下来了……
勉勉强强……用了48码，
也就是说我拿了12分。
Then my Rover stopped...
Just... In 48 yards, which
means I get 12 points.

765
00:38:53,333 --> 00:38:55,400
然后，不可思议的是，
And then, amazingly,

766
00:38:55,433 --> 00:38:57,267
杰里米那台沃尔沃，
简直就像是
Jeremy's Volvo,
as an advertisement

767
00:38:57,300 --> 00:39:00,433
防抱死刹车系统优势的活广告，
34码就刹停了。
for the advantages
of anti-lock brakes,
stopped in 34.

768
00:39:00,467 --> 00:39:05,700
这意味着他轻轻松松
捞到了26分。
Which means he gets
a very handy 26 points.

769
00:39:05,733 --> 00:39:08,133
那么，
进入下一个挑战。
And so,
for our next challenge.

770
00:39:08,733 --> 00:39:11,633
谢了。
Thank you.

771
00:39:11,667 --> 00:39:16,267
“车上每坏一样电器设备，
就扣一分。”
"Each car loses a point
for every electrical item
that isn't working."

772
00:39:16,300 --> 00:39:18,267
防抱死刹车。
能用吗，理查德？
Anti-lock brakes.
Are they working, Richard?

773
00:39:18,300 --> 00:39:20,933
-呃，这个嘛……不能。
其实根本没法……不能。
-行，扣一分。
-Uh, well... No.
They're not actually... No.
-Right. That's one off.

774
00:39:20,967 --> 00:39:22,400
把引擎盖打开。
Get the bonnet up.

775
00:39:22,433 --> 00:39:24,167
克拉克森：噢，瞧瞧！
CLARKSON: Oh, look!

776
00:39:24,200 --> 00:39:26,533
-引擎盖下面的机舱灯是坏的。
-那又怎样？无所谓。
-This under bonnet light
doesn't work.
-So what? It doesn't matter.

777
00:39:26,567 --> 00:39:28,533
天哪，全烂透了！
Oh, my God, it's all broken!

778
00:39:28,567 --> 00:39:32,067
还有你的空调也得扣一分，
因为空调也是坏的。
Now your air conditioning
as well, that's a point off,
because that doesn't work.

779
00:39:32,067 --> 00:39:34,067
雨刮器能动，
车灯能亮……
The wipers work,
the lights work...

780
00:39:34,067 --> 00:39:37,967
-但车内顶灯不亮，就是不亮。
-车内顶灯坏了。
-But the interior light
doesn't. It just doesn't.
-Interior light doesn't work.

781
00:39:38,067 --> 00:39:39,467
它就是坏的。
It doesn't work.

782
00:39:39,500 --> 00:39:41,567
行了，公布成绩。
Right enough. The results.

783
00:39:42,933 --> 00:39:45,433
理查德的罗孚……
Richard's Rover...

784
00:39:45,467 --> 00:39:47,067
三处故障，得分是……
Three faults. Giving him...

785
00:39:47,067 --> 00:39:49,833
负三分。
Minus three points.

786
00:39:49,867 --> 00:39:51,533
我的奥迪。
My Audi.

787
00:39:51,567 --> 00:39:53,067
负四分。
Minus four points.

788
00:39:53,067 --> 00:39:58,933
而杰里米的沃尔沃
找回了“真实水平”，
拿下负十二分。
And Jeremy's Volvo
back on form with
minus 12.

789
00:39:58,967 --> 00:40:02,467
现在该进行
终极测试了。
Now it's time
for the final test.

790
00:40:02,500 --> 00:40:05,233
谢谢。
呃，来了啊。
Thank you.
Uh, here we go.

791
00:40:08,400 --> 00:40:11,967
好了，伙计们。
你们最好过来瞅一眼这个。
Okay, chaps.
You might want to come
and have a look at this.

792
00:40:12,067 --> 00:40:13,733
我念了啊，上面写的是……
Here goes. What it says is...

793
00:40:13,767 --> 00:40:18,067
“你们每人必须驾驶自己的车，
以30英里的时速
撞向一堵墙。”
"Each of you must
drive your car into a wall
at 30 miles an hour."

794
00:40:18,067 --> 00:40:19,467
-哈蒙德：哈？
-对。
-HAMMOND: Eh?
-Yeah.

795
00:40:19,500 --> 00:40:21,167
-“当场毙命扣10分……”
-行吧。
-"You lose 10 points
if you're killed..."
-Okay.

796
00:40:21,200 --> 00:40:23,167
“每骨折一处
扣5分。
"Five points
for each broken bone.

797
00:40:23,200 --> 00:40:25,500
“每有一处见血伤
扣1分。”
"And one point
for each blood injury."

798
00:40:25,533 --> 00:40:28,133
-好吧，这也……
-说实话，我现在淡定得很。
-Right. That's...
-I'm feeling quite relaxed,
actually.

799
00:40:28,167 --> 00:40:29,533
-就凭你那台沃尔沃？
-就凭我的沃尔沃。
-With your Volvo?
-With my Volvo.

800
00:40:29,567 --> 00:40:31,933
我可信不过我这台罗孚，
浑身上下全特么是铁锈，
What I can't trust is my Rover
made entirely of rust,

801
00:40:31,967 --> 00:40:33,200
我心里有点发毛。
I'm feeling a bit scared.

802
00:40:33,233 --> 00:40:34,900
-詹姆斯，你没事吧？
-（杰里米大笑）
-James, are you all right?
-(JEREMY LAUGHING)

803
00:40:34,933 --> 00:40:36,367
-撞车了？
-对。
-Have a crash?
-Yeah.

804
00:40:36,400 --> 00:40:38,100
-故意的？
-对。
-On purpose?
-Yeah.

805
00:40:38,133 --> 00:40:40,067
他待会儿更惨，
因为他开的是那辆生锈破车。
It's gonna be worse
for him there, 'cause
he's in that rust car.

806
00:40:40,067 --> 00:40:44,067
而且是惨上加惨，因为规则上还写着，
鉴于你是最年轻的……
And doubly worse because
it also says here, that since
you're the youngest...

807
00:40:44,100 --> 00:40:46,167
-你先上。
-行吧。
-You're going first.
-Right.

808
00:40:46,200 --> 00:40:47,567
-梅：再见啦。
-你这逻辑真让人佩服。
-MAY: Goodbye.
-I admire your logic.

809
00:40:47,600 --> 00:40:49,067
-克拉克森：拜拜！
-真是谢谢你们啊。
-CLARKSON: Bye!
-Thank you.

810
00:40:54,467 --> 00:40:55,600
20，25……
20, 25...

811
00:40:56,600 --> 00:40:58,300
30，时速30英里……
30, 30 miles an hour...

812
00:40:58,333 --> 00:41:00,333
我要撞上去了。
我的天呐！
I'm going in.
Oh, my goodness!

813
00:41:02,067 --> 00:41:03,367
（哈蒙德闷哼）
(HAMMOND GRUNTS)

814
00:41:13,600 --> 00:41:17,467
呃，我觉得……
我的骨头应该都还顶用。
Well, um, my bones
all still work, I think.

815
00:41:18,067 --> 00:41:19,733
而且……
And...

816
00:41:19,767 --> 00:41:20,967
没见血。
There's no blood.

817
00:41:21,067 --> 00:41:24,067
看来主要是车子
替我扛下了所有冲击。
I think my car has borne
the brunt of it.

818
00:41:24,067 --> 00:41:26,500
表现还算不错。
下一个！
I think it did quite well.
Next!

819
00:41:31,333 --> 00:41:34,267
唉，这一生也算值了。
Well, it's been good.

820
00:41:35,867 --> 00:41:37,067
我见过乔迪·基德。
I've met Jodie Kidd.

821
00:41:38,667 --> 00:41:40,067
还见过斯蒂芬·弗雷。
And Stephen Fry.

822
00:41:48,200 --> 00:41:49,767
克拉克森：得，他挂了。
CLARKSON: Yes, he's dead.

823
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:52,633
所以，10分扣掉了。
So, that's 10 points
away there.

824
00:41:52,667 --> 00:41:54,533
电视机前的观众要是想来Top Gear上班，
And if you want a job
on Top Gear,

825
00:41:54,567 --> 00:41:58,100
-请写信至Top Gear……
-等等，先别急……
瞧，他缓过来了。
-please write to Top Gear...
-No, no, wait...
Look, he's coming round.

826
00:41:58,133 --> 00:41:59,300
-还真是！
-他还活着！
-He is!
-He's alive!

827
00:41:59,333 --> 00:42:01,267
-克拉克森：活过来了！
-（哈蒙德欢呼）
-CLARKSON: He lives!
-(HAMMOND CHEERING)

828
00:42:01,300 --> 00:42:03,733
那这10分就扣不成了。真扫兴。
That's no 10 points off,
though. Blast.

829
00:42:03,767 --> 00:42:06,933
这大概是我这辈子
干过最难受的事了。
The was probably
the most unpleasant thing
I've ever done.

830
00:42:06,967 --> 00:42:10,267
克拉克森：
接着轮到我了。
但我遇到了个难题。
CLARKSON:
Then it was my turn.
And I had a problem.

831
00:42:10,300 --> 00:42:14,733
车速表坏了。
所以我只能全凭感觉盲猜
30英里到底有多快。
The speedo wasn't working.
So I had to guess
how fast 30 was.

832
00:42:14,767 --> 00:42:16,533
结果我估计得稍微有点偏差。
And I got it a bit wrong.

833
00:42:18,400 --> 00:42:20,167
冲啊！
Geronimo!

834
00:42:30,300 --> 00:42:33,133
该死。该死。
我好像没撞上墙。
Damn. Damn.
I think I missed the wall.

835
00:42:37,400 --> 00:42:41,067
总之，我们都捡回了小命。
但车子怎么样了？
We all lived, then.
But what about the cars?

836
00:42:41,067 --> 00:42:43,367
理查德的罗孚彻底报废了。
Richard's Rover is dead.

837
00:42:44,067 --> 00:42:46,533
詹姆斯的奥迪也报废了。
James's Audi is dead.

838
00:42:47,500 --> 00:42:49,133
但我这辆沃尔沃呢？
But my Volvo?

839
00:42:53,067 --> 00:42:54,167
漂亮！
Yes!

840
00:42:55,767 --> 00:42:57,267
（掌声）
(APPLAUSE)

841
00:42:59,067 --> 00:43:03,167
行了行了！好啦好啦。
行行行。
Yeah, yeah! All right.
Okay, okay.

842
00:43:03,200 --> 00:43:05,967
好吧，你的车确实挺能扛，
真棒。
Okay. So your car worked.
Great.

843
00:43:06,067 --> 00:43:10,500
但你人可废了，
因为我好不容易搞到了
这个……
But you didn't,
because I have managed
to secure this...

844
00:43:10,533 --> 00:43:13,200
X光片。瞧瞧……
你觉得这是什么，杰里米？
X-ray, now...
What do you think
that is, Jeremy?

845
00:43:13,233 --> 00:43:17,533
-这是一只手的X光片。
-没错，更具体点说，
是你撞车之后的手。
-It's an X-ray of a hand.
-It is, more specifically,
your hand after that crash.

846
00:43:17,567 --> 00:43:19,733
-以40英里时速撞击后的手。
-行行行，随便你怎么说。
-That crash
at 40 miles an hour.
-Yeah. Whatever.

847
00:43:19,767 --> 00:43:21,900
关键是这块儿，看好了。
The important thing
is this bit. Look.

848
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:24,333
大拇指，骨折了！
The thumb, it's broken!

849
00:43:24,367 --> 00:43:26,333
-才没有！
-明明就有，你拇指骨折了！
-No, It isn't.
-It is. You broke your thumb!

850
00:43:26,367 --> 00:43:28,133
-詹姆斯，这算骨折吗？
-梅：骨折了。
-James, Is that broken?
-MAY: It's broken.

851
00:43:28,167 --> 00:43:29,800
哈蒙德：就是骨折了。
HAMMOND: It is.

852
00:43:29,833 --> 00:43:31,567
-只是磕掉了一点骨头茬！
-噢！听听！
-It's chipped.
-Oh! Look!

853
00:43:31,600 --> 00:43:34,667
要是茶杯磕掉一个角，
我妈都会说
它坏了。
If a tea cup is chipped,
my mother would say
it's broken.

854
00:43:34,700 --> 00:43:35,867
可不是嘛，绝对算坏了。
Absolutely, it's broken.

855
00:43:35,900 --> 00:43:37,633
就是坏了，认了吧杰里米，
你大拇指骨折了。
It is, Jeremy accept it.
You broke your thumb.

856
00:43:37,667 --> 00:43:42,067
按规则扣五分。
所以扣掉五分之后，
你的总分……
That's five points off.
So, minus five, which
brings your score...

857
00:43:42,100 --> 00:43:43,600
哈蒙德：
要是我没算错的话……（嘟囔）
HAMMOND:
If I'm right... (MUMBLES)

858
00:43:43,633 --> 00:43:46,633
折腾了这么大半天，
直接归零。
After all that
we've just done to 0.

859
00:43:46,667 --> 00:43:48,267
哈蒙德：一分都没了！
HAMMOND: No points at all!

860
00:43:48,300 --> 00:43:51,233
但还剩最后一项挑战，
也是最重磅的一项……
But there is
one challenge left.
And it is the big one...

861
00:43:51,267 --> 00:43:53,133
那就是购车成本。
It is the cost.

862
00:43:53,167 --> 00:43:57,233
规则是，在最初的一百镑预算里，
我们每省下一英镑
Now, we earn a point
for every pound we've saved

863
00:43:57,267 --> 00:44:00,100
就能加上一分。
from our original £100 budget.

864
00:44:00,133 --> 00:44:03,167
杰里米，你现在是零蛋，
已经出局了。
Jeremy, you have no points.
You're out of it.

865
00:44:03,200 --> 00:44:05,567
我有25分，哈蒙德，
而你只有10分。
I've got 25, Hammond.
You've got 10.

866
00:44:05,600 --> 00:44:09,133
-所以哪怕只差15镑，战局都会逆转。
-对，没错。
-So 15 quid either way
could swing this.
-Yeah. Yeah.

867
00:44:09,167 --> 00:44:10,633
-准备好了吗？
-妥了。
-Are you ready?
-Yep.

868
00:44:10,667 --> 00:44:12,500
我拿到我那台车的发票了。
I have the receipt for my car.

869
00:44:12,533 --> 00:44:13,567
-行。
-给你。
-Okay.
-Here.

870
00:44:13,600 --> 00:44:14,867
快看啊。
Come on.

871
00:44:14,900 --> 00:44:17,333
-快念，快念！
-我花了……
-Tell me. Tell me.
-And I spent...

872
00:44:17,600 --> 00:44:19,633
75英镑！
£75!

873
00:44:19,667 --> 00:44:21,167
好，75镑。
Right, £75.

874
00:44:21,200 --> 00:44:23,067
那只要我比你还便宜15镑……
So if I can be £15
under that...

875
00:44:23,067 --> 00:44:25,067
呃，我花了……
Um, I've spent...

876
00:44:25,100 --> 00:44:26,133
80英镑！
£80!

877
00:44:26,167 --> 00:44:27,767
这就意味着詹姆斯领先了！
Which means James is ahead!

878
00:44:27,800 --> 00:44:29,233
噢不！这也意味着……
Oh, no! Which means...

879
00:44:29,267 --> 00:44:33,367
杰里米，除非你买车只花了差不多十块钱……
Jeremy, unless you've
got your car for about £10...

880
00:44:33,400 --> 00:44:35,500
否则最后的赢家就是詹姆斯了。
James is going
to be the winner.

881
00:44:35,533 --> 00:44:36,533
-天哪！
-不会吧。
-Oh, no!
-Oh, no.

882
00:44:39,100 --> 00:44:40,467
一英镑！
£1!

883
00:44:41,167 --> 00:44:42,733
才一镑！
£1!

884
00:44:42,767 --> 00:44:44,367
(观众欢呼)
(AUDIENCE CHEERS)

885
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:46,900
太爽了！
Yes!

886
00:44:50,333 --> 00:44:52,133
全世界都在看……
The whole world...

887
00:44:52,167 --> 00:44:53,933
一群卢瑟！
Losers!

888
00:44:56,433 --> 00:44:58,133
大卢瑟！
Losers!

889
00:45:00,267 --> 00:45:01,833
不过呢，
There is, however,

890
00:45:01,867 --> 00:45:04,600
关于这几台车
还有最后两句话
得交代交代，
just a couple more things
we need to say
about these cars

891
00:45:04,633 --> 00:45:06,133
才能进入下一项。
before we move on.

892
00:45:06,167 --> 00:45:08,833
首先啊，
我们真没作弊，听懂没？
First of all,
we didn't cheat, okay?

893
00:45:08,867 --> 00:45:12,400
这台沃尔沃实际上
是我拜托一个女性朋友
替我买回来的。
I actually got a friend
of mine to go and buy
this Volvo for me.

894
00:45:12,433 --> 00:45:15,067
她从车行回来的时候，
And she came back
from the dealership

895
00:45:15,067 --> 00:45:16,533
-一共就花了一镑。
-一英镑？！
-having spent a quid.
-A pound!

896
00:45:16,567 --> 00:45:17,900
对！就一镑钱！
Yes! A quid!

897
00:45:17,933 --> 00:45:21,067
而且她简直不敢相信
自己能挑的车居然有那么多。
So, she couldn't believe
how much choice she had.

898
00:45:21,067 --> 00:45:23,500
满地都是宝马、奥迪，
还有各式各样的福特。
There were BM's and Audi's
and Ford's of all sorts.

899
00:45:23,533 --> 00:45:25,833
但市面上之所以充斥着这么多便宜车，
是有充分原因的。
But there's a very good
reason for all these cars
being around.

900
00:45:25,867 --> 00:45:27,600
因为就在没多少年前，
It is because,
not so many years ago,

901
00:45:27,633 --> 00:45:30,700
要是你的车彻底开报废了，
又破又烂，
if your car was finally broken
and old and ruined,

902
00:45:30,733 --> 00:45:33,067
你把它开进废车场，
人家还会给你二十镑。
you took it to the scrap yard
and they'd give you 20 quid.

903
00:45:33,067 --> 00:45:34,800
这事儿就算了了。
That was the end
of the matter.

904
00:45:34,833 --> 00:45:39,067
可现在呢，欧盟规定
老车必须进行回收，
这意味着，
Now though, the EU says
old cars have to be recycled,
which means,

905
00:45:39,100 --> 00:45:43,433
你得大老远把它送去报废厂，
还得倒贴给废品收购商一百镑，
you have to take it
to the scrap yard and pay
the scrap dealer 100 quid

906
00:45:43,467 --> 00:45:45,233
求人家帮你把这破烂接盘。
to take it off your hands.

907
00:45:45,267 --> 00:45:47,700
一点没错，所以我那朋友
走进那家沃尔沃
授权经销商时，
Exactly, so when this friend
of mine went into the Volvo
main dealer,

908
00:45:47,733 --> 00:45:49,600
他们刚好通过置换
收了这辆破车。
who'd taken this
as part exchange.

909
00:45:49,633 --> 00:45:52,233
车行本来想甩掉它，
得倒贴150镑，
Okay, so he had
to get rid of it,
cost him 150 quid,

910
00:45:52,267 --> 00:45:54,667
结果她走上去说：
“我给你一镑钱。”
she goes and says,
"I'll give you a quid."

911
00:45:54,700 --> 00:45:56,967
经销商反倒净赚了151镑！
He's £151 up!

912
00:45:58,600 --> 00:46:00,467
-就一镑钱！
-可不是嘛。
-A quid!
-Absolutely.

913
00:46:00,500 --> 00:46:01,600
哈蒙德：扯淡！
HAMMOND: No!

914
00:46:02,767 --> 00:46:04,500
接下来该聊聊
赛道日了。
Got to move on now
to track days.

915
00:46:04,533 --> 00:46:07,067
呃，这玩意的核心概念
其实特简单。
Uh, the idea behind this
is very simple.

916
00:46:07,067 --> 00:46:10,300
你开着自己的车
去银石、布兰兹哈奇、
多宁顿，随便哪儿……
You take you own car
to Silverstone Browns,
Donningtons, wherever...

917
00:46:10,333 --> 00:46:13,067
风驰电掣狂飙几圈，
等到了傍晚
再自己开回家。
Flash it round,
and then drive home
in the evening.

918
00:46:13,100 --> 00:46:15,233
这如今可是一桩大买卖，
规模大到什么地步呢，
It's huge business now,
so big in fact,

919
00:46:15,267 --> 00:46:18,267
甚至有车企专门造车，
that some car companies
are actually making cars,

920
00:46:18,300 --> 00:46:21,100
就为了赛道日
量身定制。
specifically designed
for the job.

921
00:46:26,367 --> 00:46:29,633
克拉克森：
这就是保时捷 GT3 RS。
CLARKSON:
This is the Porsche GT3 RS.

922
00:46:29,667 --> 00:46:33,633
它确实提供了多种颜色可选，
不过仅限轮毂。
And it comes with
a choice of colours,
but only for the wheels.

923
00:46:33,667 --> 00:46:37,267
车身颜色你能选的
就只有白色。
The only colour you can have
for the body is white.

924
00:46:40,067 --> 00:46:45,267
去年我在节目里开过一辆普通版 GT3，
当时简直爱死它了。
I drove a standard GT3
on the show last year
and I absolutely loved it.

925
00:46:45,300 --> 00:46:49,833
所以实在很难想象，
保时捷究竟还能
怎么把它改得更好。
So it's hard to see really,
how Porsche could possibly
make it better.

926
00:46:50,700 --> 00:46:52,500
但这并没能拦住他们
去瞎折腾。
But that hasn't stopped
them trying.

927
00:46:54,367 --> 00:46:58,800
本质上，他们就是拿来一辆 GT3，
然后逼它疯狂节食减重。
In essence they took a GT3
and put it on a diet.

928
00:46:58,833 --> 00:47:01,133
发动机的部分部件换成了钛合金，
They used titanium
for bits of the engine,

929
00:47:01,167 --> 00:47:03,600
弹簧是钛的，
甚至连轮毂螺栓都是钛的。
the springs
and even the wheel nuts.

930
00:47:05,900 --> 00:47:08,367
引擎盖是碳纤维的，
The bonnet is carbon fibre,

931
00:47:08,400 --> 00:47:10,067
而后车窗……
and the rear window...

932
00:47:10,067 --> 00:47:12,233
是塑料的。
That's plastic.

933
00:47:12,267 --> 00:47:16,933
为了让你们体会到
这套减重计划到底有多丧心病狂，
To give you an idea of just
how serious this weight loss
programme has been,

934
00:47:16,967 --> 00:47:19,600
看看车标。
通常保时捷车标都是珐琅金属的，
look at the badge.
It's normally enamel
on a Porsche,

935
00:47:19,633 --> 00:47:21,267
但在这台车上……
but on this...

936
00:47:21,300 --> 00:47:22,667
就只是一张贴纸。
It's a sticker.

937
00:47:22,700 --> 00:47:26,200
说真的，
我穿着一身衣服开着它到处晃，
You know,
I'm going to feel guilty
driving around in this

938
00:47:26,233 --> 00:47:28,067
都觉得挺有罪恶感的。
in my clothes.

939
00:47:28,100 --> 00:47:31,233
理想状态下，我应该光着膀子裸奔开。
Ideally, I should do it naked.

940
00:47:35,400 --> 00:47:37,533
那么，最终折腾出个什么玩意儿？
So, what have
we ended up with here?

941
00:47:37,567 --> 00:47:40,567
这么说吧，它绝对跟“舒服”不沾边。
Well, it's not what
you'd call comfy.

942
00:47:41,600 --> 00:47:43,067
我昨晚一路开到这儿，
I came down here last night

943
00:47:43,100 --> 00:47:46,967
这赛车桶椅差点没把我老腰给震断。
and this racing seat
gave me chronic back ache.

944
00:47:48,067 --> 00:47:49,900
还有那底盘悬挂。
And then there's the ride.

945
00:47:49,933 --> 00:47:52,067
说真的，哪怕把我绑在车屁股后头，
Honestly, it would have
been more comfortable

946
00:47:52,100 --> 00:47:55,167
脸贴着地一路拖过来，
都比坐车里舒服！
to have been towed behind it,
on my face!

947
00:47:56,933 --> 00:48:00,900
（哼哧声）
这样就爽多了。
(GRUNTING)
This is better.

948
00:48:04,100 --> 00:48:05,267
但是……
But...

949
00:48:05,300 --> 00:48:10,433
这是一个大写的、震耳欲聋、
中气十足的“但是”。
And it's a big, loud,
full-bodied "but."

950
00:48:10,467 --> 00:48:14,800
一旦你把它弄上赛道，
这一切就全他娘的说得通了。
When you get it to a track,
it all starts to make sense.

951
00:48:17,267 --> 00:48:20,433
它的动力感觉就像是用烈火……
It actually feels like
it's been powered with fire...

952
00:48:20,467 --> 00:48:21,767
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

953
00:48:21,800 --> 00:48:23,567
和硫磺炼出来的一样。
Brimstone.

954
00:48:23,600 --> 00:48:29,000
乔治·克鲁尼以为
自己经历过所谓的“完美风暴”。
George Clooney thought
that he had experienced
The Perfect Storm.

955
00:48:29,033 --> 00:48:31,067
他真该来开一把这车试试。
He should have had a go
in one of these.

956
00:48:32,133 --> 00:48:34,933
过弯反应简直电光火石。
The turning
is absolutely electric.

957
00:48:34,967 --> 00:48:38,267
车头绝对是指哪打哪。
Nose goes exactly
where you want it to.

958
00:48:38,300 --> 00:48:40,367
虽说它连牵引力控制都没有，
And although you don't
get traction control,

959
00:48:40,400 --> 00:48:44,067
但你根本不需要，
因为它的抓地力简直强得离谱。
you don't need it,
because there is so much grip.

960
00:48:45,500 --> 00:48:51,233
作为纯粹的驾驶体验，
这车真的挑不出一丝毛病。
As a driving experience
this really is hard to fault.

961
00:48:51,267 --> 00:48:54,133
不过，它确实有个问题。
It does, however,
have one problem.

962
00:48:58,267 --> 00:49:00,867
法拉利也造了一台赛道版跑车。
Ferrari has made
a track car too.

963
00:49:01,633 --> 00:49:05,067
隆重欢迎360 CS登场。
Welcome to the 360 CS.

